WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.060
- I just wish that you
guys could smell this

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.183
because this smells really,
really good. (sniffing)

00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:08.566
(air exhaling)

00:00:08.566 --> 00:00:11.149
(joyful music)

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.520
Hey, what's up? My name is Tway

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.960
and welcome to a special holiday
edition of Making It Big,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.850
the show where my friends challenge me

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.580
to make their favorite foods big.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.420
Now you might notice

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.540
that my table is a little
bit weird and curved.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.990
That's because we are
shooting everything in VR.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.940
You can watch the full VR episode

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.880
with a Meta Quest two in Mega Tasty.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.560
That's our virtual cooking world

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.013
within Horizon Worlds or on Meta Quest TV.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.970
Today I have a superstar in the house.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:45.870
I think she's here.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:46.840
Hi, friend, are you here?

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:47.733
- I am.
- Hi!

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.180
You guys it is-
- Hello, my love.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.740
- I'm gonna set this down.
- Thuy.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.140
- Welcome to my kitchen. Happy holidays.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.070
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.200
This is like a dream come
true for me right now.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.033
- Thanks for being here.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:00:59.866
Okay.
- I'm so excited.

00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:01.320
- Well, I'm so nervous.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.153
- I'm nervous too.

00:01:02.153 --> 00:01:02.986
But you what-
- Why are you nervous?

00:01:02.986 --> 00:01:05.110
- Because I have something
very special here.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.630
- Okay.
- And very dear.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.920
- Dang.
- And I'm excited

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.960
for you to see and uncover what this is.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.790
- Okay, let's see what it is.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:13.040
- Here we go, everybody.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:13.873
(dazzling music)

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.976
Little Debbie's Christmas cake.

00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:17.160
(Tway laughs)
(bells jingling)

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.030
- So I've never
(Thuy laughs)

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.930
had this before.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.790
Can I kind of like take a look

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.623
at what's inside-
- Yes,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:23.571
I want to smell it too. (sniffs)

00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:24.987
(Tway laughs)
- Nostalgia.

00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:25.820
(crowd cheering)

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.450
- Well you want me to make this big.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.790
How big were you thinking?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.350
- Like here?

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.760
Is that too much?

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.593
- [Crowd] Yes!

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.700
- Well, I don't have an oven that big

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.320
but I will try to-
(Thuy hums)

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.749
make it that big.

00:01:38.749 --> 00:01:40.230
(Thuy hums and giggles)

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.400
What do I need to hit here?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.410
- It needs white chocolate crust.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.840
Extra points, if you
can do extra sprinkles

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.800
and then.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.360
- And then what?
- You have to do

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.384
the iconic box that it comes in.

00:01:50.384 --> 00:01:52.620
- (gasps) Okay well I have a lot of faith

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.560
in the art department team.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.540
- Okay, okay.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.930
- I have a lot of work to
do so I will see you later.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.770
- Good luck.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.000
- Thank you. I-
- I can't wait.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.979
to see.
- I need it.

00:02:00.979 --> 00:02:01.845
- (giggles) Okay, bye.

00:02:01.845 --> 00:02:02.869
- I'll see ya later.

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:04.230
- (giggles) Bye.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:05.670
- All right guys,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.810
(enchanting music)

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.863
let's make it big.

00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:11.724
(bells jingling)

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.590
Right now I'm about to make
the first layer of the cake.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.980
As you can see there is a lot
of butter for just one layer.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.260
There's actually two layers of this cake.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.220
Whole lot of butter.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.120
Whole lot of sugar.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.780
And again, this is only
one layer of the cake.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.150
The butter gets nice and
combined with the sugar.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.030
(mixer fumbles)
(laughs)

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.093
This poor little mixer.

00:02:35.093 --> 00:02:36.960
(dreadful music)

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.060
I want to just like jump in

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.833
and start swimming around in here.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:44.790
So this is actually 48 egg yolks.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.270
I'm just going to add it in slowly.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.721
Just look at this.

00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:51.060
(gasps) I just wish

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.260
that you guys could smell this

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.576
because this smells really,
really good. (sniffs)

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:57.409
(air exhaling)

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.430
A tablespoon of almond extract,

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.310
1/2 cup of vanilla extract,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.513
eight cups of milk,

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.810
18 cups of flour.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.190
I don't like measurements.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.900
I just kind of like feeling it out.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.540
I just like to measure with my heart.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.910
But I can't, you can't do that in baking.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.973
It's a science so I have to get it right.

00:03:19.752 --> 00:03:22.502
(cheerful music)

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.060
This is the mold that
we are going to be using

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.134
for our first layer of cake.

00:03:30.134 --> 00:03:32.820
(grunts)

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.820
Okay, let's do this.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.003
I can't see.

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.490
(gasps) I hope I'm doing it right.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.323
- [Crowd] Yes.

00:03:39.323 --> 00:03:42.900
- Both of these cake layers
are gonna go into the oven

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.760
at 300 for two hours.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.343
(joyful music)

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.200
(logo swooshes)

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.710
And so to make a meringue,

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.870
it's egg whites and sugar.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.380
I just need to cook this
until it reaches 160

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.376
and then I can use the mixer.

00:04:01.376 --> 00:04:02.370
(alarm dings)

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.113
Oh my God (gasps), thank you.

00:04:05.354 --> 00:04:06.187
I love this.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.073
(joyful music)

00:04:11.431 --> 00:04:12.639
(tools clanging)

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:15.939
(joyful music)

00:04:15.939 --> 00:04:17.250
(Tway sighs)
(joyful music)

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:18.180
Okay.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:22.830
That looks like a beautiful
batch of meringue.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.230
So I'm gonna add some-
(hand slaps)

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.387
butter, duh.

00:04:27.387 --> 00:04:29.730
(drums tapping)

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:33.846
I have my vanilla extract
and my almond extract here.

00:04:33.846 --> 00:04:35.550
(machine whizzing)

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.034
And then more butter.

00:04:38.034 --> 00:04:40.701
(drums banging)

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.400
Yes.
(trumpet blaring)

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.640
Okay, I'm gonna-
(record freezes)

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.595
Excuse me.

00:04:48.595 --> 00:04:49.428
(techno music)

00:04:49.428 --> 00:04:50.520
You gotta keep going, girl.

00:04:52.092 --> 00:04:53.850
(dramatic music)

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.140
So I'm gonna leave this going.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.462
I'm gonna check on my cakes
because I think they're ready.

00:04:58.462 --> 00:05:01.212
(dramatic music)

00:05:04.453 --> 00:05:06.000
(frosting splattering)

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.710
Making these two giant cakes,

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:10.410
I feel like I can open up a bakery,

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.843
maybe call itwickery. (laughs)

00:05:13.843 --> 00:05:15.945
(dramatic music)

00:05:15.945 --> 00:05:17.070
(hands shuffling)

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:17.903
I'm ready.

00:05:17.903 --> 00:05:20.790
I gotta flip this onto here.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.781
Beryl, please help me.

00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:25.531
(dramatic music)

00:05:28.896 --> 00:05:30.325
(paper ripping)

00:05:30.325 --> 00:05:31.599
Okay, ASMR time.

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:34.266
(paper peeling)

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.050
Wasn't that so satisfying?

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.930
Okay so this is the fun part.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:43.023
I am going to be cutting out the tree.

00:05:43.921 --> 00:05:47.760
(knife scratching)
(twinkling music)

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.020
Oh.
(record freezes)

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.000
My God, don't cut yourself.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.035
I did cut myself (whimpers).
(dramatic music)

00:05:53.035 --> 00:05:55.200
- [Camera Director] Okay,
time for a band-aid.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.729
This just turned into a medical show.

00:05:56.729 --> 00:06:01.729
(ambulance blaring)
(dramatic music)

00:06:02.894 --> 00:06:05.775
- Do not try this at home.

00:06:05.775 --> 00:06:07.650
(dramatic music)

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:11.250
Yep. And we have a
Little Debbie cake tree.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.301
- [Crowd] Yes.

00:06:12.301 --> 00:06:14.884
(joyful music)

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.570
- All right, so my cake is in the freezer.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:23.010
I want it nice and cold for me
to pour the chocolate on top.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:26.370
So in the meantime, I'm
going to make sprinkles.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.940
I think this is the most satisfying part

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.843
of whipping something up
because of the little patterns.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:37.800
I just kind of like stare at it

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.176
and like get in a little trance.

00:06:40.176 --> 00:06:41.296
(bright music)

00:06:41.296 --> 00:06:42.723
Oh, yes.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.118
Grinch green.

00:06:45.118 --> 00:06:48.120
(joyful music)

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.481
It's kind of fun.

00:06:49.481 --> 00:06:50.723
(machine buzzing)

00:06:50.723 --> 00:06:53.306
(joyful music)

00:06:55.408 --> 00:06:56.811
Ready?

00:06:56.811 --> 00:06:58.726
- [Computer Voice] One, two three, four,

00:06:58.726 --> 00:07:02.369
five, six, seven, eight, nine ten.

00:07:02.369 --> 00:07:04.290
(audience clapping)

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.198
- A few hours later, my
sprinkles have hardened.

00:07:07.198 --> 00:07:08.031
(Tway gasps)

00:07:08.031 --> 00:07:10.864
(paper crinkling)

00:07:11.795 --> 00:07:14.878
(sprinkles breaking)

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:16.913
Let me taste.

00:07:18.073 --> 00:07:19.170
- [Crowd] Oh yeah.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:20.850
- That tastes like a sprinkle.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:22.263
A big sprinkle.

00:07:23.147 --> 00:07:25.730
(upbeat music)

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.367
I gotta work fast.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:32.950
(upbeat music)

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.470
All right I still have some
more corners to cover over here

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:46.290
and then I'll be ready to decorate.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.897
Finally.

00:07:47.897 --> 00:07:48.730
(record scratching)

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.300
(upbeat music)

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:55.110
So I'm gonna start off with
sprinkling on my sprinkles.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.580
They're just kind of like everywhere

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.750
so I'm going to add them everywhere.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.880
You don't wanna mess up this piping bag.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.770
Consistency is everything.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.175
Yes.
(crowd cheering)

00:08:06.175 --> 00:08:08.253
(fingers snapping)
Tway-casso.

00:08:09.758 --> 00:08:12.508
(tranquil music)

00:08:14.042 --> 00:08:15.120
(claps) Okay.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:17.763
This is the moment I've
been waiting for all day.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.773
Made the box,

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.723
made the cake.

00:08:22.575 --> 00:08:24.780
(gasps) I'm ready for the judgment.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.474
Thuy, come on in, please.

00:08:26.474 --> 00:08:27.667
(drums tapping)
- Are you ready for me?

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:29.199
- Yes.

00:08:29.199 --> 00:08:30.838
(joyful music)

00:08:30.838 --> 00:08:33.180
(Tway screams)
- The ca-

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.980
Yo. Killed it.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.877
But this is amazing.

00:08:36.877 --> 00:08:37.710
(bells jingling)

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.210
Oh, it says Tasty Tway.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.060
- Yeah.
- Oh my God that is so cute.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:42.893
- Okay so one

00:08:42.893 --> 00:08:43.726
of the challenges was-
- Yes.

00:08:43.726 --> 00:08:44.559
- to make the box.

00:08:44.559 --> 00:08:45.392
- Right.
- So?

00:08:45.392 --> 00:08:46.225
- Okay, you,

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.058
you got the points.
(whistle blows)

00:08:47.058 --> 00:08:47.891
- Turn around.

00:08:47.891 --> 00:08:48.966
- Okay.

00:08:48.966 --> 00:08:52.230
(cheerful music)

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:53.553
Holy.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.130
(laughing)

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:56.963
- Are you ready?

00:08:56.963 --> 00:08:58.350
- I'm ready.
- To taste this.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.905
- I'm ready, I haven't
had dessert all day.

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:00.871
(both laughing)

00:09:00.871 --> 00:09:01.704
So I'm ready.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.740
- We also made extra sprinkles

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:07.803
because you had wanted
the extra sprinkles.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.060
This cake is 50 pounds by the way.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.223
Do you see that crust?
- Oh my God.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.133
Ready?
- Cheers.

00:09:16.133 --> 00:09:16.966
- Cheers.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:19.967
(Thuy moaning)

00:09:19.967 --> 00:09:20.933
- Tway, this is really good.
(crowd cheering)

00:09:20.933 --> 00:09:21.766
- Thank you,
- I'm to proud of you.

00:09:21.766 --> 00:09:22.599
- Thank you.

00:09:22.599 --> 00:09:24.720
- Thank you so much for challenging me.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.880
This was really, really fun to make.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.328
Let me know what I should make big next

00:09:29.328 --> 00:09:31.046
(camera clicking)
and I'll see you next time.

00:09:31.046 --> 00:09:31.879
(camera clicking)
Peace out.

00:09:31.879 --> 00:09:34.696
